<concept id="t00624">
	<title>Auto Highway Speed Change</title>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e03881">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e03882">
								<image href="images/OCL4M055127N.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<ol outputclass="callout" id="e03883">
								<li>
									<p><uicontrol>Driver Assistance</uicontrol></p>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p><uicontrol>Driving Convenience</uicontrol></p>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p><uicontrol>Auto Highway Speed Change</uicontrol></p>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>While the vehicle is <term translate="no">ON</term>, tap <menucascade><uicontrol>Setup</uicontrol><uicontrol>Vehicle</uicontrol><uicontrol>Driver Assistance</uicontrol><uicontrol>Driving Convenience</uicontrol><uicontrol>Auto Highway Speed Change</uicontrol></menucascade> on the infotainment system screen.</p>
		<note type="tip" id="e03884">
			<p>If there is a problem with Navigation-based Smart Cruise Control, you cannot turn the function <term translate="no">ON</term> in the settings menu.</p>
		</note>
	</conbody>
	<related-links>
